hexagon: reject a GDN chain when a replaced tensor has a reader in a different split
Fold-into: patches/hexagon-fusion/0007-hexagon-htp-gdn-fusions-with-rollback-slots.patch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The fused GDN_CONV_STEP does not write the GET_ROWS, the CONCAT and the
SSM_CONV of its chain. The fused GDN_STATE_STEP does not write the
GET_ROWS of its chain or the state tail of the GATED_DELTA_NET output. The
matcher looked for other readers of these tensors only in the nodes of the
split that graph_compute gets. Thus a reader in a later split got bytes
that no op wrote. For example, a SCALE of the CONCAT in a later split read
the bytes of an earlier tensor, and a reader of the state tail in a later
split read bytes that no op wrote.

The split that graph_compute gets is a view of the full graph
(ggml_graph_view), and the view shares the hash set and the use counts of
the full graph. ggml_build_forward_expand counts the uses, and the splits
of ggml_backend_sched are views of that graph. This patch compares the use
count of each such tensor, and of each member view of it, with its uses in
the split. When the two counts are different, a node of a different split
uses the tensor, and the matcher rejects the chain. A graph with no use
counts gets no fused GDN op.

The count of the uses in the split occurs in the loop that the matcher
already has, and only for a source of an intermediate or of the output.
Thus the time of the match does not change: the first packing of the
decode graph takes the same time with and without this patch (about 630
us for the 2B and 1050 us for the 4B on x86). The model graphs of the app
have no such reader. hexhost_graphs gives the same ops with and without
this patch on the decode, prefill, MTP and image paths of the 2B and the
4B. The comment at the top of htp-gdn-match.h describes this rule in place
of the split limit of the state chain.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h
index 910dcaa..8b25def 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h
@@ -13,10 +13,12 @@
 // other reader of the replaced tensors, and no other node that touches the cache inside the chain span.
 // The state_zero SCALE of build_rs comes before the chain, thus it stays a separate op and runs first.
 //
-// The matcher sees only the nodes of the split that graph_compute gets. The fused state op does not
-// write the state tail of the GATED_DELTA_NET output, thus the only permitted reader of that tail is
-// the CPY into the cache in the same split. A reader in a later split gets bytes that no op wrote. The
-// model graphs have no such reader: tests/fuzz/hexhost/run.sh graphs checks the paths of the app.
+// The matcher sees only the nodes of the split that graph_compute gets. The fused ops do not write the
+// replaced tensors (GET_ROWS, CONCAT, SSM_CONV) or the state tail of the GATED_DELTA_NET output. Thus a
+// reader of such a tensor in a different split gets bytes that no op wrote. The split is a view of the
+// full graph, and it has the use counts of the full graph. The match compares the use count of each
+// such tensor with its uses in the split, and it rejects the chain when a use is in a different split.
+// A graph with no use counts gets no fused op.
 //
 // This header depends on ggml only. A host program can run the same checks on a graph. Each check
 // returns nullptr when the chain matches, or a short text for the first failed condition.
@@ -123,8 +125,24 @@ static inline std::unordered_map<const ggml_tensor *, int> ggml_hexagon_gdn_inde
     return index;
 }
 
+// The use count of t in the full graph, or -1 when the graph has no use count for t. The split that
+// graph_compute gets is a view of the full graph (ggml_graph_view), and the view shares the hash set
+// and the use counts of the full graph. Thus the count includes the uses in the other splits.
+static inline int32_t ggml_hexagon_gdn_graph_uses(const ggml_cgraph * gf, const ggml_tensor * t) {
+    if (!gf->use_counts || !gf->visited_hash_set.used || gf->visited_hash_set.size == 0) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+    const size_t pos = ggml_hash_find(&gf->visited_hash_set, t);
+    if (pos == GGML_HASHSET_FULL || !ggml_bitset_get(gf->visited_hash_set.used, pos)) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+    return gf->use_counts[pos];
+}
+
 // Every node that reads an intermediate (also through a view) must be a member of the chain. A view of
-// `out` is permitted for any node when the view lies in the first `out_head_bytes` bytes of `out`.
+// `out` is permitted for any node when the view lies in the first `out_head_bytes` bytes of `out`. No
+// node of a different split can use an intermediate or `out`, or a member view of them.
+// O(nodes * GGML_MAX_SRC * members).
 static inline const char * ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private(const ggml_cgraph * gf,
                                                              const std::vector<ggml_tensor *> & intermediates,
                                                              const std::vector<ggml_tensor *> & members,
@@ -137,6 +155,21 @@ static inline const char * ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private(const ggml_cgraph *
     if (out && (out->flags & GGML_TENSOR_FLAG_OUTPUT)) {
         return "the output is a graph output";
     }
+    // The fused op does not write these tensors: the members with an intermediate or `out` as root.
+    // Each one gets the count of its uses in this split. Such a use has an intermediate or `out` as
+    // root, thus only the two branches of the loop below count.
+    std::vector<std::pair<const ggml_tensor *, int32_t>> unwritten;
+    for (ggml_tensor * m : members) {
+        ggml_tensor * root = ggml_hexagon_gdn_root(m);
+        if (ggml_hexagon_gdn_contains(intermediates, root) || (out && root == out)) {
+            unwritten.emplace_back(m, 0);
+        }
+    }
+    auto count_use = [&unwritten](const ggml_tensor * src) {
+        for (auto & u : unwritten) {
+            u.second += u.first == src ? 1 : 0;
+        }
+    };
     for (int i = 0; i < gf->n_nodes; i++) {
         ggml_tensor * n = gf->nodes[i];
         for (int s = 0; s < GGML_MAX_SRC; s++) {
@@ -146,6 +179,7 @@ static inline const char * ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private(const ggml_cgraph *
             }
             ggml_tensor * root = ggml_hexagon_gdn_root(src);
             if (out && root == out) {
+                count_use(src);
                 // The region that the reader touches: the view node itself when n is a view of out
                 // (its src is the whole tensor), else the view that n reads.
                 const ggml_tensor * region = (src == out && ggml_hexagon_gdn_is_view_op(n)) ? n : src;
@@ -157,11 +191,24 @@ static inline const char * ggml_hexagon_gdn_chain_is_private(const ggml_cgraph *
                 }
                 return "the state part of the output has a reader outside the chain";
             }
-            if (ggml_hexagon_gdn_contains(intermediates, root) && !ggml_hexagon_gdn_contains(members, n)) {
-                return "an intermediate has a reader outside the chain";
+            if (ggml_hexagon_gdn_contains(intermediates, root)) {
+                if (!ggml_hexagon_gdn_contains(members, n)) {
+                    return "an intermediate has a reader outside the chain";
+                }
+                count_use(src);
             }
         }
     }
+    // A use that the full graph counts and this split does not have is a reader in a different split
+    for (const auto & u : unwritten) {
+        const int32_t uses = ggml_hexagon_gdn_graph_uses(gf, u.first);
+        if (uses < 0) {
+            return "the graph has no use count for a replaced tensor";
+        }
+        if (uses != u.second) {
+            return "a replaced tensor has a reader in a different split";
+        }
+    }
     return nullptr;
 }
 
